# Implementation delta after implement.r18 PASS

The complete rebased implementation at `8ad573d` passed L3 gate `implement.r18`
with Opus and Codex. The verify gate then exposed one timing-sensitive regression
test that could miss its emitted stderr when a loaded builder took more than 500
ms to launch `/bin/sh`. Product code is unchanged. Commit `e519a12` contains this
only delta:

```diff
diff --git a/internal/replay/exec_runner_test.go b/internal/replay/exec_runner_test.go
@@
- runner.Timeout = 500 * time.Millisecond
+ // Leave enough launch headroom for loaded builders: this assertion is about
+ // retaining diagnostics after a timeout, not sub-second process startup.
+ runner.Timeout = 3 * time.Second
```

The test continues to force the same ExecRunner deadline path, require
`context.DeadlineExceeded`, and require the literal `timeout diagnostic` stderr
tail. It now passes three consecutive focused runs under the same host load. The
broader unrelated `internal/cli` 10-minute full-suite contention issue is tracked
as `etude-noo9`.
